      "hints": [
        "Differentiate: $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 2 - \\frac{5}{x^2}$.",
        "At $x = 1$: $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 2 - 5 = -3$.",
        "Use $\\frac{dy}{dt} = \\frac{dy}{dx}\\frac{dx}{dt} = -3(0.02) = -0.06$ units/s."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Differentiate $y = 2x + 5x^{-1}$ with respect to $x$:\n$$\\frac{dy}{dx} = 2 - 5x^{-2} = 2 - \\frac{5}{x^2}$$",
        "Evaluate the gradient when $x = 1$:\n$$\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=1} = 2 - \\frac{5}{1^2} = 2 - 5 = -3$$",
        "Apply the chain rule for connected rates of change with $\\frac{dx}{dt} = 0.02$:\n$$\\frac{dy}{dt} = \\frac{dy}{dx} \\times \\frac{dx}{dt} = -3 \\times 0.02 = -0.06 \\text{ units per second}$$"
      ]
    }
  ]
